# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Coverage instrumentation output (the instrumented test binaries write these
# into the current directory when `cargo llvm-cov` runs)
*.profraw

# Reference code (separate project)
laya/

# Node (Playwright GUI smoke)
node_modules/

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Agent process state (plans, specs, SDD progress)
/.superpowers/

# Local runtime state written by `agent` (event logs, artifacts, smoke runs)
/.agent-data/
/.agent-smoke*/

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
credentials.*
*private*key*
*token*
*secret*

# `agent-store-secret` is a source crate (a SecretProvider adapter), not a
# credential file, so exempt it from the broad `*secret*` ignore above.
!crates/agent-store-secret/

# The port `SecretProvider` is defined in is source too. Without this line the
# broad pattern above silently keeps it out of git: the file builds locally and
# is missing from every fresh clone.
!crates/agent-ports/src/secret_provider.rs

# The same hazard again for the argument-resolution module split out of
# `guarded.rs` when the permission gate pushed it past its ratchet: it reads
# references, it holds no credential.
!crates/agent-kernel/src/secret_refs.rs

# And once more for `guarded`'s split-out test module. It exercises reference
# resolution and holds no credential; ignored, the crate's tests would not
# compile in a fresh clone.
!crates/agent-kernel/src/guarded/tests/secrets.rs

# The GUI's design tokens are a stylesheet, not a credential. The broad
# `*token*` pattern above would keep it out of git; the page then builds locally
# and fails on a fresh clone with a missing `@import`.
!web/src/styles/tokens.css

# Local kernel-eval output (reports and transcripts from live runs)
/apps/agent/kernel-eval-*.json
/apps/agent/target/

# 本机的启动配置（可能含密钥），不要提交
scripts/gui/start.local.ps1

# Personal package output
scripts/personal/dist/
